  "step_1": "The decision reason evaluates skewness of the lotteries, specifically defining a lottery as right-skewed when a greater portion of probability is assigned to unfavorable outcomes (i.e., 0 Euros) compared to favorable outcomes (i.e., positive amounts). However, in both Lotteries A and B, the favorable outcome (positive amount) is 6000 or 3000 Euros, and the unfavorable outcome is 0 Euros. The probability of getting 0 Euros is 55% in A and 10% in B. Thus, A has a much larger portion of probability assigned to the unfavorable outcome (0 Euros), making it more right-skewed. The reason prefers the more right-skewed lottery, which in this case would be Lottery A. Therefore, the decision reason is applicable to the problem and can be evaluated based on the probabilities and outcomes provided.",
