  "step_3": "The decision reason is based on skewness — specifically, the proportion of probability assigned to unfavorable outcomes. The individual does not mention or evaluate the distribution of probabilities across outcomes in terms of skewness. Instead, the individual focuses on the magnitude of losses and the time required to recover from them, which reflects a risk-aversion or loss-recovery perspective, not a skewness-based evaluation. The comparison of probabilities of negative outcomes (e.g., 25% vs. 50%) is not discussed, nor is there any reference to the shape of the distribution. Therefore, the individual did not apply the skewness-based decision reason. The justification is based on loss magnitude and recoverability, not on the skewness of the lottery. Hence, the decision reason was not used.",
